###  http://www.semanticweb.org/sanar/ontologies/2026/0/miao-validation#ICD-11
:ICD-11 rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                 <https://w3id.org/miao#MentalIllnessesSchema> ;
        <https://w3id.org/miao#hasMentalIllnessCategory> <http://www.semanticweb.org/sanar/ontologies/2026/0/miao-validation#6A02-AutismSpectrumDisorder> ,
                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/sanar/ontologies/2026/0/miao-validation#6A20-Schizophrenia> ,
                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/sanar/ontologies/2026/0/miao-validation#6A6Z-BipolarOrRelatedDisordersUnspecified> ,
                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/sanar/ontologies/2026/0/miao-validation#6B00-GeneralisedAnxietyDisorder> ,
                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/sanar/ontologies/2026/0/miao-validation#6D10-PersonalityDisorder> ,
                                                         <http://www.semanticweb.org/sanar/ontologies/2026/0/miao-validation#6A7Z-DepressiveDisordersUnspecified> ;
        <https://w3id.org/miao#usedInMentalIllnessesDetection> :CNNAnxietyDetection ,
                                                               :CNNAutismDetection ,
                                                               :CNNBPDDetection ,
                                                               :CNNBipolarDetection ,
                                                               :CNNDepressionDetection ,
                                                               :CNNSchizophreniaDetection ,
                                                               :XGBoostAnxietyDetection ,
                                                               :XGBoostAutismDetection ,
                                                               :XGBoostBPDDetection ,
                                                               :XGBoostBipolarDetection ,
                                                               :XGBoostDepressionDetection ,
                                                               :XGBoostSchizophreniaDetection ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "World Health Organization (WHO): https://www.who.int/" ;
        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> 11 ,
                                              """International Statistical Classification of Diseases and Related Health Problems (ICD) s the international standard for systematic recording, reporting, analysis, interpretation and comparison of mortality and morbidity data. This 11th revision (ICD-11) is the result of an unprecedented collaboration with clinicians, statisticians, classification
and IT experts from around the world, making it useable by these groups, as well as by coders. ICD–11 allows countries to count and identify their most pressing health issues by using an up-to-date and clinically relevant classification system. Health conditions and accidents are assigned ICD–11 codes, resulting in data that can be used by governments to design effective public health policies, and measure their impact, or used for clinical recording. For the first time, ICD is fully electronic, currently providing access to 17 000 diagnostic categories, with over 100 000 medical
diagnostic index terms. The index-based search algorithm interprets more than 1.6 million terms. ICD–11 is easy to install and use online or offline, using free 'container' software. https://icd.who.int/en/""" .


